#4471 contains three distinct date problems, not one. The export has overlapping pages, so
counts below use unique report IDs. The cause classifier follows the tenant locale and booking
form; the five one-day-move reports are separated using the support desk's own notes.

<Incident4471Breakdown />

## 1. Shared parser reads month first

For day-first locales, the shared parser flips day and month. This is the main issue in #4471
after the separately identified one-day moves are removed. It affects reports across tenants
and channels, so grouping only by subject or intake tag would hide the common cause.

## 2. Booking-v3 date hint conflicts with tenant locale

In booking-v3, the field hint is `MM/DD/YYYY`. People follow that hint, but the form reads the
date according to the tenant's day-first locale. These reports need a separate fix from the
shared parser: changing the parser does not correct what the form tells people to enter.

## 3. Five one-day moves need separate investigation

The support desk's `desk-notes.json` identifies five reports as one-day moves. Their descriptions
include an invite arriving before a booking, different days for Lisbon and Toronto, and a
Tuesday/Monday shift. Keep them out of the month-flip ticket until timezone and timing behavior
are understood.

## Triage recommendation

File one issue per problem. Keep the report counts from the component above, link the five
one-day-move report IDs in their issue, and do not treat intake tags as verified causes: they
are guesses and disagree with tenant/form classification.

